# Build-context exclusions.
#
# The important one is `.env`: without it, `docker build` would send the API token to the
# daemon and bake it into a layer, which is the one thing invariant I8 exists to prevent
# (docs/DECISIONS.md D23, D73). This file is a security control, not tidiness.

# Secrets and runtime state
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
data/

# Local environment and caches
.venv/
.git/
.gitignore
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.hypothesis/
.coverage
htmlcov/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]

# The image installs from pyproject.toml/uv.lock, src/ and config/. Copying the whole tree would
# add ~800 KB of test fixtures — including the 749 KB Persian book — for nothing.
#
# README.md is deliberately NOT excluded, despite being documentation: pyproject.toml declares
# `readme = "README.md"`, so the build backend opens it and `uv sync` fails without it. Found by
# running the container's own install steps locally rather than trusting this file to be right.
tests/
docs/
scripts/
plan.md
AGENTS.md
refactor-plan.md
Makefile

# The image is not a build toolchain: no dev group, no test runner.
.dockerignore
Containerfile